  "result": "I've written the plan but haven't changed any code, because plan mode is on. I couldn't call ExitPlanMode (it isn't available here), so I'm asking for approval in this message instead.\n\n**Cause:** `split_arg_string` in `src/click/shell_completion.py:623` builds a `shlex.shlex` lexer. shlex treats `#` as a comment start by default, so everything after an unquoted `#` is dropped. For example, `cli a #foo b` becomes `[\"cli\", \"a\"]`. All four shells (bash, zsh, fish, powershell) go through this function, so all of them are affected. I haven't run it; this comes from reading the code and shlex's documented behavior.\n\n**Planned fix:**\n1. Add `lex.commenters = \"\"` after `lex.whitespace_split = True` in `split_arg_string`.\n2. Add a `CHANGES.md` entry.\n3. Add regression tests:\n   - Cases in `tests/test_parser.py::test_split_arg_string`: `\"cli a #b c\"` and `\"cli a#b\"`.\n   - An end-to-end case in `tests/test_shell_completion.py::test_full_complete`.\n4. Verify by running `pytest tests/test_parser.py tests/test_shell_completion.py`, and confirm the new tests fail without the fix.\n\nI'm leaving out the fact that the shell scripts don't escape `#` or commas in completion values. That's a separate issue.\n\nThe full plan is in `<home>\\.claude\\plans\\shell-completion-gives-wrong-zazzy-glacier.md`. Reply to approve it and I'll implement it.",
